May 15, 2026 - Version 1.50

Notes
-----
Since mid-2025 the WMF has been clamping down on API requests due to a flood of AI bots.
This was mostly solveable with a well-formed User-Agent string.
Beginning in 2026 this was not enough, by March 2026 the 429s become extreme.
Experiments showed that API read requests that used OAuth authentication did better.
The changes in 1.50 are mostly about making the system more stable in this way.
OAuth consumer keys are freely available and can be generated on the fly - it is highly recommended
in the world of AI scraper overload. Obtain keys (see EDITSETUP), put them in a safe text file, link
the text file location at the top of wikiget as explained in the source code. Finally, turn on OAuth by default
with G["oauth_read"] = 1 

New Features
----------------
-U  : This allows sending an API request through wikiget that handles the OAuth for you. Thus if you have 
      a bash, Python script etc and don't want to bother with OAuth, just system call wikiget -U 
      and it will resolve the API request using your OAuth credentials. 

            wikiget -U "action=query&meta=siteinfo&format=json"
            (fully authenticated request using your OAuth credentials)
      
-N  : Null-edit a page. 

-Y  : Show debugging info and route to target "stderr", "stdout", or a /file/path (appends).

(max) : API requests now return "max" records (5,000 for bots). This reduces the number of API requests,
        speeds up the results and reduces the chances of a 429.

-X  : Toggle Toolforge Private Proxy (default: ON/OFF).
      This is a feature I use for myself. It interfaces with custom software running on Toolforge
      to further reduce 429s. If interested in learning more drop me a message.

Function changes
----------------

allPages(): Updated the fallback pagination limit from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

apierror(): Updated the regex to safely tolerate unpredictable spaces and newlines within WMF JSON error blocks.

apiurl(): Refactored to cleanly handle custom Toolforge proxy routing, repackage OAuth headers, and include expanded retry-on-http-error definitions (429, 502, 503, 504).

apiurlPost() (NEW): Created to cleanly handle API URL building and custom proxy routing when using a file for POST data.

backlinks(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 250/500 to the dynamic "max" value.

BEGIN (Global Config): Hardened default wget options to fail faster, enabled OAuth reads by default, implemented global timeout check (max 500s limits), improved missing email configuration path reporting, and initialized Toolforge proxy settings.

category(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value. Fixed transient network drop handling.

editPage(): Added stderr capture to catch blank HTTP responses during heavy load and implemented cookiejar cleanup.

getbacklinks(): Updated return limits to "max" and injected an apierror() break condition into the pagination loop.

getcategory(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

getEditToken(): Completely rewritten to include a 3-retry loop with a 5-second sleep and standard error logging for improved stability when fetching CSRF tokens.

getrdchanges(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

getrechanges(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

getucontribs(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

getxlinks(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

http2var(): Completely rewritten to support authenticated OAuth reads, custom proxy routing (repackaging Authorization to X-WMF-OAuth), dynamic maxlag escalation, and heavier linear smart retry backoff logic. Added explicit "Exhaustion Catch" logging. Regex matched Wikipedia URLs broadened to ([.]|/)wiki.

movePage(): Removed a redundant setupEdit() call to save an execution cycle and added cookiejar cleanup.

MWOAuthGenerateHeader(): Upgraded the nonce generator to a cryptographic hex string and optimized the shell piping for HMAC creation. Added strict URL decoding and re-encoding for parameters, fixed header value wrapping with double quotes, and updated the signature base string construction.

nulleditPage() (NEW): Created to issue empty edits that force MediaWiki to refresh category and template links.

Pagination Loops (Global): Multiple pagination loops (categorymembers, etc.) updated to return "" instead of break on transient network drops to safely end the fetch cycle. Fixed URL encoding on continuation parameters.

parsecommandline(): Added getopt parsing for the new -N (Null Edit), -U (Raw API), -O (Toggle OAuth), -X (Toggle Proxy), and -Y (Debug Destination) flags.

printResult(): Added arr to local scope and introduced logic to explicitly parse and report HTTP/Varnish network errors.

processarguments(): Added the routing logic to handle the actions for the new -N, -U, -O, -X, and -Y flags.

purgePage(): Added stderr capture to catch blank HTTP responses during heavy load and implemented cookiejar cleanup.

rawAPI() (NEW): Created to allow users to send custom, fully authenticated API queries directly through the terminal.

rechanges(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

redirects(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

setupEdit(): Appended the process ID (PROCINFO["pid"]) to the cookiejar file to safely allow concurrent script executions.

stdErr(): Updated to support routing output dynamically to stderr, stdout, or appending to a file based on the -Y flag debug destination.

ucontribs(): Updated the hardcoded API return limits from 500 to the dynamic "max" value.

urldecodeawk() (NEW): Added native function to decode percent-encoded strings efficiently.

urlencodeawk(): Fixed the default regex fallback to accurately match PHP's rawurlencode behavior.

usage(): Added visual help text descriptions for the new -N, -O, -U, -X, and -Y command-line flags.

usage_extended(): Added terminal usage examples demonstrating how to use the new custom API request and null edit features.

userInfo(): Refactored to cleanly output the raw JSON payload to stdout for normal CLI usage if debugging is disabled, and added cookiejar cleanup.
